.TH CCODE 1 "September 2026" "ccode v0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ccode \- terminal AI coding assistant (single binary: TUI + CLI)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ccode
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fB\-p\fR \fIPROMPT\fR | \fB\-i\fR | \fB\-\-json\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
NOTE (September 2026, temporary):
.B ccode
is paused and no longer built; only
.BR ccode-cli (1)
is shipped. This page is kept for reference.
.PP
.B ccode
is a single binary that carries both the interactive TUI and the CLI
backend in one process. A bare
.B ccode
starts the in-process TUI (the agent runs in the same process, no child
is forked); it renders the conversation in an ANSI terminal, streams
assistant output as it arrives, and shows tool permission prompts.
.PP
With
.B \-p
(one-shot prompt),
.B \-i
(interactive REPL) or
.B \-\-json
(JSON Lines backend for other frontends) it behaves exactly like
.BR ccode-cli (1).
The TUI is always interactive: no
.B \-i
or prompt flag is required to start it.
.PP
How the single binary dispatches: a bare
.B ccode
starts the in-process TUI; with
.BR \-p ,
.BR \-i ,
or
.B \-\-json
(and whenever it is invoked under a name ending in
.BR \-cli ,
e.g. via a symlink) it runs as the CLI backend instead. On Windows
consoles a redirected stdin/stdout falls back to the line REPL unless
.B \-\-tui
is given (and
.B \-\-no-tui
forces the REPL).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-api-base " URL"
OpenAI-compatible API base URL (defaults to
.BR CCODE_API_BASE ).
.TP
.BI \-\-api-key " KEY"
API key (defaults to
.BR CCODE_API_KEY ).
.TP
.BI \-\-model " NAME"
Model name (defaults to
.BR CCODE_MODEL ).
.TP
.B \-\-thinking
Send the
.B "thinking"
field
.RB ( type:
.BR enabled ).
On by default; disable with
.BR CCODE_THINKING=0 .
Independent of
.BR \-\-reasoning .
.TP
.B \-\-reasoning
Send the reasoning_effort field (default effort:
.BR high ).
.TP
.BI \-\-reasoning-effort " LEVEL"
Reasoning effort:
.BR low ", " medium ", " high ", " xhigh
or
.BR max .
Implies reasoning on.
.TP
.BI \-\-thinking-effort " LEVEL"
Alias for
.BR \-\-reasoning-effort .
.TP
.B \-\-write
Enable read and write tools (write_file, edit_file, bash, run_command,
web_fetch, ...) with interactive confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-read-only
Read-only tools (read_file, glob, grep, read_tool_output). This is the default mode.
.TP
.B \-\-default
Fast start preset: interactive UI plus read/write tools plus thinking
at
.BR high " effort."
Never enables
.BR \-\-auto-approve .
.TP
.B \-\-auto-approve
Approve every tool request without asking. Equivalent to
.BR CCODE_AUTO_APPROVE=1 .
.TP
.B \-\-allow-http
Allow
.BR http://
API endpoints beyond loopback (also
.BR CCODE_ALLOW_HTTP=1 ).
Plaintext traffic, known risk. Loopback http is always allowed.
.TP
.B \-\-no-markdown
Disable markdown rendering (raw output).
.TP
.BI \-\-backend " PATH"
Accepted; ignored by the single binary (it runs the agent in-process).
Only the split
.BR ccode-tui (1)
frontend uses it to locate its backend.
.TP
.BI \-\-save-session " PATH"
Save the conversation to
.I PATH
after each prompt.
.TP
.BI \-\-resume " PATH"
Load a conversation from
.I PATH
before the run.
.TP
.BI \-\-session-dir " DIR"
Session storage directory (defaults to
.BR CCODE_SESSION_DIR ).
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage.
.TP
.B \-\-tui
Run the in-process TUI (the default for a bare invocation; mainly
useful on Windows consoles, see DESCRIPTION).
.TP
.B \-\-no-tui
Escape hatch: force the line-based REPL instead of the TUI (used on
Windows consoles; accepted everywhere, otherwise no effect).
.SH TUI KEYS
.TP
.B Enter
Submit the input line.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-C
Cancel the in-flight request (press twice to quit).
.TP
.B Ctrl\-D / Ctrl\-Q
Quit the TUI.
.PP
Additional editing keys follow common readline conventions (arrows,
home/end, backspace, etc.).
.PP
The in-process TUI accepts the same slash commands as
.BR ccode-cli (1).
.B /compact
compacts the session chain file in place (it reports "Nothing to
compact yet." before the first turn creates one).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
See
.BR ccode-cli (1)
for the full list. Relevant to the TUI:
.TP
.B CCODE_BACKEND
Backend executable path. Ignored by the single binary; only the split
.BR ccode-tui (1)
frontend reads it.
.TP
.B CCODE_WORKSPACE
Workspace directory (defaults to the current directory).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.ccode/sessions/
Conversation session files (JSON).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ccode-cli (1),
.BR ccode-tui (1),
.PD 0
